      "writtenOn": "2021-03-05T00:29:11Z",
      "side": 1,
      "message": "There\u0027s a lot of duplicated code here. Maybe merge this test with the previous one?\n\nWhile code duplication might make it a bit easier to read each test in isolation, it makes it very hard to review the whole CL, and causes the file to become huge and unreadable quite quickly (consider: this CL by itself contributes more than 4% of the lines of this file, and this file has been around for years). Also, simple refactorings in test code become very large refactorings, and minor changes to test methods mean details like ordering, timeouts, etc. etc. drift over time. Also, all else being equal, testing multiple things in one test may be more likely to find bugs, since CS has to do more work before the test completes and the class is reinitialized.\n\nAnother option (which I don\u0027t think we\u0027ve ever attempted, though), is to put this test in a new file that is not ConnectivityServiceTest, use setUp / tearDown methods to eliminate a lot of the code duplication, and use members instead of local variables for things like NetworkCallbacks, agents, etc.\n\nWe might be able to do the same even within this file by having multiple top-level classes in it.",
      "range": {
        "startLine": 10806,
        "startChar": 0,
        "endLine": 10829,
        "endChar": 33
      },
